# tests/modifiers/reset.rxt — module `modifiers` (MOD-0.5c): the `(?^)`
# construct, per the MEASURED rule in docs/plan.md [MOD-0.5a] ruling 3 and
# tests/probes/probe_mod05b.c's "== (?^) reset scope per letter ==" block:
# `(?^)` resets i, m, n, s, x, xx to their HARDWIRED DEFAULTS (reset-to-
# constant, not reset-to-compile-option — the load-bearing PARSE-1 landmine)
# and does NOT touch U or J, both probed surviving.
#
# ORACLE: python `re` has no `(?^)` syntax at all (unknown extension, any
# position) — EVERY block here is `# pcre2-only`. Expectations are the
# match spans measured directly from tests/probes/probe_mod05b.c's own
# "(?^) reset scope per letter" cells (2026-08-12, libpcre2 10.46), plus one
# additional cell (the J-survives compile+match) measured the same way with
# a throwaway extension of that probe (scratchpad, not committed).
#
# THE J CELL IS A FORWARD PIN, NOT A §9.3 near-term flip: it needs BOTH
# `modifiers` (this module, for J/^) AND `named-groups` (for `(?<name>...)`)
# to have PRODUCERS before it can compile at all. It will stay a
# pattern-compile failure through MOD-0.5's close and only turn green once
# `named-groups` lands too — flagged here so a future reader does not read
# it going green at MOD-0.5c as a sign something else broke, or read it
# staying red past MOD-0.5c as a regression.
#
# THE D33 §9.3 RECORD: run against the MOD-0.5a-gate binary via
#   PCREC=<binary> bash tests/harness/run.sh tests/modifiers/reset.rxt
# every block's pcrec compile fails with "requires module 'modifiers'" —
# 8 cases, 0 passed, 7 distinct pattern-compile failures (measured
# 2026-08-12).

# ---- i is reset by (?^) --------------------------------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?i)a(?^)a
features modifiers
m "Aa" 0 2
n "AA"

# ---- U SURVIVES (?^) — the measured exception ----------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?U)(?^)a+
features modifiers
m "aaa" 0 1

# ---- J SURVIVES (?^) — forward pin, needs named-groups too (see header) --

# pcre2-only
pattern (?J)(?^)(?<g>a)(?<g>b)
features modifiers,named-groups
m "ab" 0 2

# ---- s is reset by (?^) ---------------------------------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?s)(?^).
features modifiers
n "\n"

# ---- n is reset by (?^): plain (...) captures again -----------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?n)(?^)(a)
features modifiers
m "a" 0 1

# ---- x is reset by (?^): whitespace no longer skipped ---------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)(?^)a b
features modifiers
n "ab"

# ---- xx is reset by (?^): class interior no longer touched ----------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)(?^)[a b]
features modifiers
m " " 0 1
